# This package is assembled, not written.
#
# `drumlin` on npm is one package carrying three executables, because the
# workspace split is a build-time concern: the bundle inlines every
# `@drumlin/*` import, so nothing resolves them at runtime. Shipping the three
# together also makes the daemon lookup in packages/client structurally sound —
# `drumlind` is always beside `drumlin` — rather than a search that can miss.
#
# So the only checked-in file here is the manifest. `pnpm build` writes the
# rest: the bundles into dist/, and copies of the README and LICENSE that npm
# needs inside the tarball to render the package page.
dist/
README.md
LICENSE
